# Composer
vendor/
composer.lock

# The seeded database is generated by `php seed.php`, not committed: it is 5 MB of
# benchmark rows, and a stale copy silently changes what every arm measures.
data/

# Harness output. A published run's raw per-repeat data is a deliverable and is
# committed (`results/raw.tsv`); everything else a run produces is per-host and
# per-run scratch.
#
# The crossover and latency passes are also named deliverables: they are the two
# passes that answer questions the sweep cannot, so their raw rows are kept alongside
# the sweep's rather than treated as scratch.
results/*.tsv
!results/raw.tsv
!results/crossover.tsv
!results/latency.tsv
# A superseded sweep is kept, not deleted: the report quotes ratios that only a
# later build can be compared against, and a comparison needs both sides.
!results/raw-*.tsv
results/*.log
!results/run.log
*.log

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
